__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Never commit anything that could hold a value. The repository stores OpenBao
# paths and logical secret-file names; the files themselves are host state.
secrets/
*.token
*.key
*.pem

# A production render resolves the private inventory, so its bytes legitimately
# carry endpoints and credential basenames (ADR-0006). `deploy/rendered/` is the
# CLI's default output directory, so an operator who runs `render` without
# `--output` writes exactly that material here. The committed render lives at
# `tests/fixtures/reference/rendered/` and is synthetic; nothing under this path
# is ever committed.
deploy/rendered/

# Any private inventory an operator fetches into the working tree. The one
# tracked instance is the synthetic fixture, which is not under this path.
private-inventory*.json

# ...but NOT a contract. `private-inventory-capture.schema.json` matched the
# glob above and was silently untracked: `make check` passed locally, because
# both scanners read `git ls-files` and an untracked file is not in it, and CI
# then failed on eight tests importing a file that had never been committed.
#
# The un-ignore is scoped to `contracts/` and to `*.schema.json` rather than
# loosening the glob, because the glob is right: an operator's fetched document
# must stay ignored wherever it lands. A SCHEMA is the opposite kind of thing —
# public by ADR-0006 §1, since a shape discloses nothing — so it is exempted by
# what it is, not by where somebody happened to put it.
!contracts/private-inventory*.schema.json
